INSERT INTO `conversations` VALUES (1,1,'New Chat','2026-10-07 08:35:01','2026-10-14 12:15:11','- **Core Topic:** JSON Web Tokens (JWT) and resume details (education, contact info, awards, and certificates).\n- **User Requests & Preferences:** The user previously asked about JWT concepts and has now asked for a full resume summary, specifically checking for awards, honors, and certificates. The user prefers simple, beginner-friendly explanations.\n- **Key Facts Covered:**\n  - JWT is a stateless, cryptographically signed digital pass consisting of a Header, Payload, and Signature.\n  - The user\'s resume highlights a Full Stack / MERN background, experience at ArhamSoft, key projects (ResumEase, Real-Time Chat App, Task Management System), and education (Bachelor of Information Engineering Technology from Superior University, 2021–2025, CGPA: 3.48/4.00).\n  - The resume does not contain contact information or mention any awards or honors.\n  - The resume includes certifications in JavaScript Full Stack / Web Development (NAVTTC), AI Fundamentals (Cisco / IBM SkillsBuild), and an Advanced Certification in JavaScript & Full Stack Development (MEAN-MERN) with an A+ grade.',300),(2,1,'New Chat','2026-10-07 12:43:54','2026-10-08 15:11:38','- **Topic:** Large Language Models (LLMs), APIs, AI engineering, chunking, hallucination, guardrails, full-stack chatbot architecture (backend code analysis including `createMessage` controller), and Database Indexing.\n- **Key Questions Asked:**\n  - How the Gemini API works (tokenization, embeddings, attention mechanism, next-token prediction).\n  - Real-world uses of the Gemini API.\n  - What the user\'s very first prompt/query was (\"check\").\n  - How to connect Gemini with the MERN stack, MySQL, and implement user authentication (JWT, bcrypt).\n  - Full-stack AI chatbot documentation and code explanation.\n  - Explanation of the uploaded documents detailing LLMs, APIs, chunking, hallucinations, guardrails, and Database Indexing.\n  - Explanation of uploaded backend code images (`createMessageService` in `messageServices.js` and the `createMessage` controller).\n  - Request for a one-line summary of the backend code.\n- **User Behavior:** Frequently types short, prompt-based commands like \"more,\" \"try,\" \"check,\" \"next,\" \"yes,\" and \"Explain this\" in response to uploaded documents and images, alongside greetings (\"hi\").\n- **Decisions & Progress:** Completed comprehensive documentation for a full-stack AI chatbot, explored core AI concepts, analyzed uploaded documents on LLMs/APIs and Database Indexing, explained uploaded snippets of backend JavaScript code for handling chatbot messages, and noted that the user asked about the `createMessage` controller image.\n- **Ongoing Tasks:** Awaiting the user to upload or attach the image of the `createMessage` controller so it can be analyzed and explained, or awaiting the user\'s next prompt, question, or file.',175),(4,2,'New Chat','2026-10-07 13:52:48','2026-10-12 14:23:38','- Topics discussed: Prompt engineering for LLM summarization, meta-prompts for updating conversation summaries, and incremental memory updating in AI applications.\n- User questions: \n  - Asked what the best prompt is for LLM summarization.\n  - Provided a specific prompt template for updating conversation summaries and asked for an evaluation of it.\n- Important facts: \n  - The best summarization prompts use a structured formula: Role, Task, Constraints, and Context/Source Text, along with guardrails to prevent hallucinations.\n  - A rolling conversation summary prompt efficiently combines a previous summary with new messages to maintain context without processing the entire chat history.\n  - Instructions like \"Return only the updated summary\" prevent conversational filler and make it easier to programmatically save summaries to a database.\n- Decisions: \n  - The AI explained the components of effective summarization prompts and provided copy-and-paste examples (executive summary, beginner-friendly, strict-fact, and length-restricted).\n  - The AI evaluated the user\'s conversation-updating prompt, highlighting why it is effective for backend memory management.\n- Ongoing tasks: \n  - Assisting the user with understanding or writing code for LLM prompts, backend architecture, or any related topics.',286),(6,1,'New Chat','2026-10-07 15:57:11','2026-10-08 14:58:57','- Important topics: Backend Development, JavaScript, Database Management, AI Integration\n- Important questions: The user shared a code snippet related to backend services, message creation, file uploads to Gemini, and database checks using Sequelize, but did not ask a specific question yet.\n- Important answers: The assistant identified the code snippet and offered help with debugging, refactoring, or explaining how it is built.\n- Ongoing tasks: Awaiting the user\'s specific question or request regarding the shared code snippet.',171),(7,1,'New Chat','2026-10-14 12:27:52','2026-10-14 12:32:56','The user repeatedly asked to identify the technologies mentioned in their resume, but they still have not uploaded or provided the text of their resume. The assistant repeatedly reminded the user to upload or paste their resume so it can be analyzed.',316),(8,1,'New Chat','2026-10-14 12:43:44','2026-10-14 12:43:44',NULL,NULL),(9,2,'New Chat','2026-10-14 12:45:03','2026-10-15 08:54:44','The user previously reviewed their resume, highlighting their Full Stack Web Developer identity, MERN internship at ArhamSoft, core skills, projects, certifications (in Chinese), and education details (in Korean). The user repeatedly asked about education starting in 2019 and awards and recognition; it was confirmed based on the resume that there is no 2019 education (only Superior University from 2021 to 2025) and no awards and recognition section listed.',354),(10,2,'New Chat','2026-10-15 08:41:42','2026-10-15 08:59:20','The user previously asked about ideal chunk sizes for RAG systems (explaining that 500 to 1,000 characters is typical) and whether the provided resume document contained awards and recognition (noting it only contains education, certifications, and project experience). The user then asked about \"Gemini Embedding 2 vs Gemini Embedding 001\" (clarifying that Google\'s official text embedding model is `text-embedding-004`) and about Gemini API rate limits (explaining RPM, TPM, RPD, free vs. paid tiers, and 429 errors). Most recently, the user asked what skills are mentioned in the resume, and the assistant listed them across frontend, backend, databases, authentication, real-time technologies, programming languages, and tools.',362),(11,2,'New Chat','2026-10-15 08:59:36','2026-10-19 14:54:41','The user previously inquired about Gemini API rate limits and requested various resume details, including education, certifications, a professional summary, and technical skills and project details. Following earlier inquiries about all project names and the second project specifically, the user recently asked for the second skill heading (\"Backend Development\"), the second-to-last skill heading (\"Tools & Platforms\"), and again asked for the second project name (\"Real-Time Chat Application — MERN Stack & WebRTC\") from the resume document.',454),(12,2,'New Chat','2026-10-15 13:58:20','2026-10-19 15:02:40','The user asked to find all projects mentioned in their resume document. The assistant identified four projects: the \"Facebook Clone — Full Stack Social Media Application\", \"Real-Time Chat Application — MERN Stack & WebRTC\", \"Task Management System — MERN Stack\", and \"ResumEase — AI-Powered HR Assistant\". The user then asked to list all the technologies used in these projects, and the assistant provided a breakdown of the specific technologies (such as React.js, Node.js, MongoDB, WebRTC, Python, and Django) used in each project based on the resume.',466),(14,2,'New Chat','2026-10-19 15:11:15','2026-10-20 08:27:54','The user discussed the projects listed in their resume, including the Facebook Clone, Real-Time Chat Application, Task Management System, and ResumEase, along with the specific technologies used in each. The user also requested and received a complete list of these technologies categorized by project. Additionally, the user inquired about their certifications, and the assistant listed them, specifically highlighting the AI Fundamentals: Foundations for Understanding AI certification from Cisco / IBM SkillsBuild (2026).',492),(16,2,'New Chat','2026-10-20 14:47:07','2026-10-20 14:53:14','The user asked to list all projects from their resume (Facebook Clone, Real-Time Chat Application, Task Management System, and ResumEase) and subsequently requested a comprehensive list of all technologies used across those projects, which was provided categorized by frontend, backend, databases, authentication, real-time tools, and file handling.',510),(17,2,'New Chat','2026-10-21 07:53:33','2026-10-21 07:53:33',NULL,NULL),(18,2,'New Chat','2026-10-21 08:01:20','2026-10-21 08:15:52','The user previously discussed sections of their uploaded resume, including four projects (Facebook Clone, Real-Time Chat Application, Task / To-Do Application, and ResumEase), three certifications, a full resume summary, and their professional experience as a MERN Stack Developer Intern at ArhamSoft. Recently, the user asked for specific details about the Facebook Clone project from their resume, followed up with a question asking what \"RLS\" (Row Level Security) means in the context of that project, and subsequently asked for an explanation of \"Score thresholding.\"',536),(19,2,'New Chat','2026-10-22 11:03:28','2026-10-23 09:33:36','The user previously asked for a list of projects from their resume (identifying Facebook Clone, Real-Time Chat Application, Task/To-Do Application, and ResumEase), certifications (NAVTTC, Cisco/IBM SkillsBuild, and Centre for Digital Literacy & Business Management), and education details (Information Engineering Technology degree from Superior University with years of study and CGPA). Recently, the user asked to see the certifications again, and then twice asked to list every project, prompting the assistant to provide details for the Facebook Clone and note that the details for the Real-Time Chat Application were cut off in the document chunks.',585),(20,2,'New Chat','2026-10-23 07:30:28','2026-10-23 09:26:43','The user repeatedly asked to list all projects from the provided resume/document. The assistant listed the projects found in the current document: \n1. Facebook Clone (with full details using React.js, Supabase, PostgreSQL, etc.).\n2. Real-Time Chat Application (mentioned by name and technologies—MERN Stack & WebRTC—with no further details due to text cut-off). \nThe assistant also noted that while other projects (Task/To-Do Dashboard and ResumEase) were mentioned in earlier conversation history, they are not present in the currently provided document text.',569),(21,2,'New Chat','2026-10-23 09:27:32','2026-10-23 09:27:32',NULL,NULL),(22,2,'New Chat','2026-10-23 09:30:32','2026-10-23 09:32:08','The user asked the assistant to list all the projects from their uploaded resume document. The assistant identified four projects: Facebook Clone (React.js, Supabase, PostgreSQL, etc.), Real-Time Chat Application (MERN Stack & WebRTC), Task/To-Do Application, and ResumEase — AI-Powered HR Assistant (Python, Django, HTML5, CSS3, Bootstrap 5, JavaScript, SQLite, AI/ML).',579),(23,2,'New Chat','2026-10-23 09:57:07','2026-10-23 09:58:41','The user asked to see the list of projects from the provided document. The assistant provided details for two projects: \n1. Facebook Clone (a full-stack social media application using React.js, Supabase, PostgreSQL, etc., with features like user auth, posts, messaging, and admin moderation).\n2. Real-Time Chat Application (mentioned as using the MERN stack and WebRTC, with further details cut off in the text).',593),(24,2,'New Chat','2026-10-23 09:58:52','2026-10-23 09:58:52',NULL,NULL),(25,2,'New Chat','2026-10-23 10:01:41','2026-10-23 10:01:41',NULL,NULL),(26,2,'New Chat','2026-10-23 10:02:47','2026-10-23 12:29:13','The user previously asked to list every project from their resume (Facebook Clone and Real-Time Chat Application) and all technologies used. The assistant provided a categorized list of technologies and a summary of the resume\'s professional profile, technical skills, and projects. The user then agreed to include additional sections, and the assistant summarized the education and project experience. Finally, the user asked to list all certifications, and the assistant provided the certifications from the document, including JavaScript Full Stack / Web Development by NAVTTC, AI Fundamentals by Cisco / IBM SkillsBuild (2026), and Advanced Certification in JavaScript & Full Stack Development (MEAN-MERN) from the Centre for Digital Literacy & Business Management with an A+ grade.',615),(27,2,'New Chat','2026-11-05 08:11:19','2026-11-05 08:11:19',NULL,NULL),(28,2,'New Chat','2026-11-05 08:47:39','2026-11-05 08:47:39',NULL,NULL),(30,2,'New Chat','2026-11-05 08:53:23','2026-11-05 08:53:23',NULL,NULL),(32,2,'New Chat','2026-11-05 09:00:37','2026-11-05 09:09:16','The user previously asked about their resume projects (Facebook Clone, Real-Time Chat App, Task Management System, and ResumEase) and requested a professional summary detailing their background as a Full Stack and MERN Stack Developer Intern at ArhamSoft. In recent messages, the user asked what JavaScript is, inquired about the certifications listed in their resume (including NAVTTC, Cisco/IBM SkillsBuild, and Centre for Digital Literacy & Business Management), and requested simple example code for JavaScript, which the assistant provided covering variables, functions, conditional statements, and arrays.',645),(33,2,'New Chat','2026-11-05 09:13:09','2026-11-05 09:13:09',NULL,NULL),(37,2,'New Chat','2026-11-05 10:48:48','2026-11-05 10:48:48',NULL,NULL),(48,3,'New Chat','2026-11-05 11:26:25','2026-11-05 11:26:25',NULL,NULL),(49,3,'New Chat','2026-11-05 11:28:10','2026-11-05 11:28:10',NULL,NULL),(51,3,'New Chat','2026-11-05 12:09:22','2026-11-05 12:09:22',NULL,NULL),(52,3,'New Chat','2026-11-05 12:11:56','2026-11-05 12:11:56',NULL,NULL),(53,3,'New Chat','2026-11-05 12:12:42','2026-11-05 12:12:42',NULL,NULL),(55,3,'New Chat','2026-11-05 12:19:58','2026-11-05 12:19:58',NULL,NULL),(56,2,'New Chat','2026-11-05 12:22:11','2026-11-05 12:22:11',NULL,NULL),(57,3,'New Chat','2026-11-05 12:23:39','2026-11-05 12:30:22','The user has requested technical explanations for machine learning, neural networks, RAG, NLP, LLMs, and exploratory data analysis, along with a comparative analysis of React and Angular. The user also requested an in-depth analysis of their resume, covering projects (Facebook Clone, Chat App, Task Management, ResumEase), technologies used, technical skills, machine learning components, education, and dates. A comparison of projects and a search for React-based projects within the resume were also provided. The user additionally inquired about neural networks and their relation to uploaded content. All previous requests have been answered. There are no ongoing tasks.',727),(58,2,'New Chat','2026-11-05 14:11:57','2026-11-05 14:18:10','The user has inquired about machine learning concepts and compared the React and Angular web development frameworks. For machine learning, key concepts discussed include supervised, unsupervised, and reinforcement learning, along with the importance of generalization and avoiding overfitting. Regarding web development, React was identified as a flexible, component-based library using the Virtual DOM, while Angular is a comprehensive framework that includes built-in tools like routing and two-way data binding. The user has requested to perform analysis on additional webpages but has not yet provided the specific URLs for those follow-up tasks.',738),(59,2,'New Chat','2026-11-10 08:08:02','2026-11-10 08:18:54','The user requested a report on the Model Context Protocol (MCP). The assistant provided an overview explaining that MCP is an open standard introduced by Anthropic in November 2024 to simplify how AI models connect to external data and tools. The assistant also provided the official MCP documentation website and Anthropic\'s announcement as source links.',743),(60,2,'New Chat','2026-11-10 08:30:02','2026-11-10 08:30:02',NULL,NULL),(63,2,'New Chat','2026-11-10 09:27:33','2026-11-10 09:27:33',NULL,NULL),(64,2,'New Chat','2026-11-10 10:36:49','2026-11-10 10:36:49',NULL,NULL),(65,2,'New Chat','2026-11-10 10:42:30','2026-11-10 10:42:30',NULL,NULL),(66,2,'New Chat','2026-11-10 10:47:42','2026-11-10 10:47:42',NULL,NULL),(72,2,'New Chat','2026-11-10 13:14:57','2026-11-10 13:18:00','The user asked what artificial intelligence (AI) is. The assistant explained that AI is the simulation of human intelligence in machines, covered how it works using data and patterns, outlined subfields like machine learning and natural language processing, distinguished between narrow and general AI, and provided everyday examples such as virtual assistants and recommendation systems.',791),(73,2,'New Chat','2026-11-10 13:19:00','2026-11-10 13:19:00',NULL,NULL),(74,2,'New Chat','2026-11-10 13:44:28','2026-11-10 13:44:28',NULL,NULL),(75,2,'New Chat','2026-11-10 13:45:39','2026-11-10 13:45:39',NULL,NULL),(76,2,'New Chat','2026-11-11 13:08:12','2026-11-11 13:18:32','The user inquired about the differences between AI and Machine Learning and requested a JavaScript string-reversal function. The assistant summarized four projects from the user\'s resume: a Facebook Clone, a Real-Time Chat Application, a Task Management Dashboard, and ResumEase. The user asked for details regarding the second section of the resume, which the assistant identified as \"Technical Skills.\" The user also requested information on the history of Python, which the assistant provided using Wikipedia sources. Finally, the user asked for a definition of a topic within their uploaded resume; the assistant clarified that the document is a resume and lacks general topic definitions, requesting further clarification from the user.',818),(77,2,'New Chat','2026-11-11 14:07:38','2026-11-11 14:10:16','The user is a Full Stack Web Developer and MERN Stack Developer Intern at ArhamSoft (July 2026–Present) with a Bachelor’s in Information Engineering Technology. Their technical expertise includes React.js, Node.js, Python, MongoDB, and PostgreSQL. They have built a portfolio featuring a Facebook clone, a real-time chat application with WebRTC, an AI-powered HR tool (ResumEase), and a task dashboard. The user requested an overview of their projects, a general resume summary, and specific details regarding their professional experience.',824),(78,2,'New Chat','2026-11-11 14:11:24','2026-11-11 14:56:47','The user requested a list of all projects from their resume. The assistant successfully extracted four projects: Facebook Clone, Real-Time Chat Application, Task Management Application, and ResumEase. The user specifically inquired about the technologies used in the Facebook Clone, which the assistant detailed (React.js, Bootstrap 5, Supabase, PostgreSQL, and related security/real-time tools).',840),(79,2,'New Chat','2026-11-11 14:56:49','2026-11-11 15:00:11','The user is asking for the technologies used in a \"Facebook Clone\" project listed on their resume. The assistant has searched the provided documents but could not find any mention of a project by that name or a similar description. The assistant has requested that the user provide the specific text from the resume or more context to allow for an analysis.',846),(80,2,'New Chat','2026-11-11 15:02:42','2026-11-11 15:34:22','The user\'s projects include a Facebook Clone (React.js, Bootstrap 5, Supabase), a Real-Time Chat Application (React.js, Node.js, Express.js, MongoDB, Mongoose, Socket.IO, WebRTC, and JWT), and ResumEase (SQLite, AI-powered HR recruitment features like resume screening, data extraction, interview scheduling, skill matching, and a recruiter dashboard). The assistant does not have access to the user\'s personal information, such as their home address. No information regarding the user\'s favorite programming language is available.',859),(87,1,'What is Artificial Intelligence? Explain...','2026-11-12 13:51:35','2026-11-12 13:51:37',NULL,NULL),(88,1,'Tell me about Albert Einstein using Wiki...','2026-11-12 13:54:10','2026-11-12 13:54:13',NULL,NULL),(89,1,'MERN Job Resume Comparison','2026-11-12 13:57:16','2026-11-12 13:57:26',NULL,NULL),(90,1,'Python Statistics Calculation','2026-11-12 14:18:19','2026-11-12 14:21:11','The user requested the calculation of the mean, median, and standard deviation for the dataset [10, 20, 30, 40, 50]. The assistant provided Python code using the `statistics` module to compute these values, noting the difference between sample and population standard deviation. The results are: Mean (30), Median (30), Population standard deviation (≈14.14), and Sample standard deviation (≈15.81).',910),(91,1,'Python Stats Calculation','2026-11-12 14:28:30','2026-11-12 14:28:32',NULL,NULL),(93,2,'Understanding EDA','2026-11-13 13:30:57','2026-11-13 13:33:23','The user inquired about the definition of Exploratory Data Analysis (EDA), which involves examining and visualizing datasets to identify patterns, anomalies, and data quality issues before formal modeling. Additionally, the user requested summaries of two uploaded documents: a research paper on \"Supabase,\" which details its role as an open-source backend-as-a-service (covering authentication, PostgreSQL, and Row Level Security), and a guide titled \"EDA (1).pdf,\" which outlines the objectives, steps, and multivariate analysis techniques involved in the EDA process.',919),(94,2,'Understanding EDA','2026-11-13 13:39:34','2026-11-13 13:39:37',NULL,NULL),(95,2,'EDA vs Supabase Comparison','2026-11-13 13:42:45','2026-11-13 13:47:09','The user inquired about the relationship between Event-Driven Architecture (EDA) and Supabase, clarifying that EDA is a design pattern while Supabase is a Backend-as-a-Service (BaaS) platform. They can be used together, particularly through Supabase\'s features like Webhooks, Realtime, and Edge Functions. The user also explored Row-Level Security (RLS), learning that it is a database-level security feature used to restrict data access by user, which acts as an \"invisible WHERE clause.\" The user specifically referenced a document titled \"Research on SupaBase.pdf\" to understand how RLS functions within the Supabase ecosystem compared to traditional backend security methods.',933),(96,2,'Purpose of Feature Engineering','2026-11-13 13:48:28','2026-11-13 13:48:32',NULL,NULL),(97,1,'Understanding EDA Concept','2026-11-13 13:55:01','2026-11-13 13:55:16',NULL,NULL),(99,2,'Explaining EDA Steps','2026-11-13 14:17:39','2026-11-13 14:21:08',NULL,NULL),(100,2,'Supabase vs EDA Comparison','2026-11-13 14:25:39','2026-11-13 14:26:00',NULL,NULL),(101,2,'The provided documents do not contain information ','2026-11-16 07:26:50','2026-11-16 07:27:37',NULL,NULL),(103,2,'REST vs GraphQL APIs','2026-11-16 07:36:05','2026-11-16 07:42:23','The user has inquired about the differences between REST APIs and GraphQL, the definition and importance of Exploratory Data Analysis (EDA) in machine learning, and a comparison between the purposes of EDA and Supabase. The user also clarified that the provided information did not come from their uploaded documents.\n\n*   **REST vs. GraphQL:** REST uses multiple endpoints and fixed structures, while GraphQL uses a single endpoint for more efficient, client-specific data requests.\n*   **EDA:** A diagnostic phase in data science involving statistical summaries and visualizations to understand, clean, and identify patterns in data before modeling.\n*   **Supabase:** An open-source backend-as-a-service platform providing tools like PostgreSQL, authentication, and real-time APIs to simplify app development.\n*   **Fact:** The capital of Japan is Tokyo.\n*   **Status:** The assistant clarified that it does not currently have access to the user\'s uploaded documents and offered to use them if explicitly requested.',963),(104,2,'Understanding LLM APIs','2026-11-16 07:45:52','2026-11-16 07:50:10','The user requested an explanation of the differences between REST API and GraphQL, which was provided using a restaurant analogy comparing fixed menus (REST) to customizable ingredient-based ordering (GraphQL). The user also asked for a comparison of Event-Driven Architecture (EDA) and Supabase; it was clarified that EDA is a design pattern for decoupling systems, while Supabase is a Backend-as-a-Service platform. The two can be used together, such as using Supabase database triggers to initiate event-driven tasks.',971),(105,2,'Understanding LLM Operations','2026-11-16 07:52:48','2026-11-16 07:58:19','The user asked for an explanation of the differences between REST APIs and GraphQL, but the assistant could not provide this information as it was not in the provided document context. The user also asked for a definition of Exploratory Data Analysis (EDA), which the assistant defined as the process of examining and visualizing data to understand its contents, quality, and patterns. Key aspects of EDA covered include its purposes (understanding data, quality check, distribution, relationships), applications (market analysis, risk assessment, etc.), and types (univariate, bivariate, and multivariate).',977),(106,2,'REST API vs GraphQL','2026-11-16 08:04:51','2026-11-16 08:15:11','The user previously requested an explanation of REST vs. GraphQL and an overview of Exploratory Data Analysis (EDA). The user then asked to list the projects from their uploaded resume, which the assistant identified as a Facebook Clone, Real-Time Chat Application, Task/To-Do Application, and ResumEase. Subsequently, the user asked for specific EDA techniques, which the assistant provided, confirming that the information was based on general knowledge rather than the user\'s uploaded documents.',989),(107,2,'LLM Context Management Basics','2026-11-16 08:18:25','2026-11-16 08:38:52','The user inquired about Exploratory Data Analysis (EDA) and the differences between REST API and GraphQL.\n\nRegarding EDA, the assistant explained it as a process of examining, cleaning, and visualizing data to uncover patterns and prepare it for machine learning. Techniques are categorized into univariate, bivariate, and multivariate analysis.\n\nRegarding REST versus GraphQL, the assistant clarified that REST uses multiple endpoints with fixed data structures, while GraphQL uses a single endpoint where clients request specific data. The summary includes a comparison table highlighting differences in data fetching, versioning, and complexity to help determine which approach is better suited for specific application needs.',995),(108,2,'Exploratory Data Analysis','2026-11-16 08:46:26','2026-11-16 08:46:32',NULL,NULL),(109,4,'AI vs Agentic AI','2026-11-16 08:53:18','2026-11-16 08:54:49','The user inquired about the difference between standard AI and agentic AI, noting that standard AI acts as a tool for specific tasks while agentic AI functions as an autonomous assistant capable of planning and using tools to reach goals. The user also requested an explanation of Exploratory Data Analysis (EDA), specifically its purpose and techniques (univariate, bivariate, and multivariate). Finally, the user asked for a summary of the projects listed on their resume, which include a Facebook clone, a real-time chat application, a task/to-do dashboard, and an AI-powered HR assistant named ResumEase.',1003);
