stem, user, assistant).\n3. **Context & Context Windows:** Explains how models remember past conversation history, how attention mechanisms connect related words, and the limits of how much text a model can process at once.\n4. **Tokens:** Defines tokens as pieces of text processed by the model and how token generation works statistically.\n5. **Chunking:** Explains how large documents are broken into smaller, searchable pieces (chunks) with overlaps to maintain context for precise retrieval.\n6. **Chunking and Hallucination:** Relates how document chunks work together with tokenization and vector embeddings.\n7. **Hallucination:** Discusses when AI makes things up, why it happens, and how to fix it.\n8. **Guardrails:** Outlines safety systems used to validate inputs and outputs, restrict topics, and protect sensitive data.\n\n---\n\n### **What is written under the \"Hallucination\" heading?**\n\nAccording to section **8) Hallucination** in the document:\n\n* **Definition:** Hallucination occurs when an AI generates information that is false, fabricated, or unsupported by the available evidence/context, while presenting it as if it were valid.\n* **Why does hallucination happen?**\n  1. **Pattern Matching:** The AI predicts the next likely word instead of checking the facts.\n  2. **Missing Knowledge:** If the AI doesn\'t know the true answer, it tries to fill in the blank by guessing what sounds right.\n  3. **Bad Data:** The internet has mistakes, which the AI learns during training.\n  4. **Outdated Knowledge.**\n* **How do we reduce hallucination?**\n  1. **Give Real Facts First (RAG):** Connect the AI to a safe search tool or document library so it reads real documents instead of guessing from its memory.\n  2. **Fine-Tuning:** Train the AI on clean, professional data rather than random websites.','2026-10-09 07:41:59','2026-10-09 07:41:59',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'null',0),(182,4,'user','and what\'s under the guardrails','2026-10-09 07:42:42','2026-10-09 07:42:42',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'null',0),(183,4,'assistant','Based on the uploaded document, here is what is written under the **Guardrails** heading (which is section 9 in the file):\n\n### **Guardrails**\n\n* **Definition:** Guardrails are safety systems or filters placed around an AI model to make sure its inputs (what the user types) and outputs (what the AI replies) are safe, appropriate, and accurate.\n* **What do Guardrails do?**\n  1. **Block bad inputs:** Stop inappropriate questions, hate speech, or prompt injection attacks before they reach the AI.\n  2. **Keep the AI on topic:** Prevent the AI from talking about things it shouldn\'t (for example, a medical chatbot refusing to give financial advice).\n  3. **Filter toxic outputs:** Catch offensive language, hate speech, or harmful instructions before the user sees them.\n  4. **Protect privacy:** Block sensitive data like credit card numbers or passwords from being shared.','2026-10-09 07:42:44','2026-10-09 07:42:44',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'null',0),(184,4,'user','total number of words and pages','2026-10-09 07:43:07','2026-10-09 07:43:07',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'null',0),(185,4,'assistant','Based on the uploaded document, I cannot answer this request because the file does not contain information about the total number of words or pages.','2026-10-09 07:43:08','2026-10-09 07:43:08',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'null',0),(186,4,'user','can you count?','2026-10-09 07:43:24','2026-10-09 07:43:24',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'null',0),(187,4,'assistant','Yes, I can count words if you provide text or a document! \n\nHowever, looking at the document you previously uploaded, it only contains the specific sections and text we\'ve been discussing (like Hallucination and Guardrails), but it does not include metadata about the total page count or word count. \n\nIf you would like me to count the words in the text currently available from the document, I can certainly do that for you. Just 