,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'null',0),(360,10,'assistant','Gemini API rate limits depend on the specific model you are using and whether you are using the free tier or a paid (pay-as-you-go) tier through Google AI Studio or Google Cloud Vertex AI. \n\nHere is a breakdown of how rate limits generally work for the Gemini API:\n\n### 1. Key Rate Limit Terms\n*   **RPM (Requests Per Minute):** How many times you can call the API per minute.\n*   **TPM (Tokens Per Minute):** The maximum number of tokens (words/pieces of words) you can send and receive combined per minute.\n*   **RPD (Requests Per Day):** The maximum number of requests allowed in a 24-hour period (common on free tiers).\n\n### 2. General Tiers\n*   **Free Tier:** Designed for experimentation and testing. It comes with stricter limits (for example, lower RPM and RPD) and data may be used to improve Google products depending on the specific terms of the service you use.\n*   **Paid Tier (Pay-As-You-Go):** Designed for production applications. It offers significantly higher RPM and TPM limits so your app can handle more traffic.\n\n### 3. Current Limits (Example for Flash/Pro Models)\n*Because limits can change and vary by model version (like Gemini 1.5 Flash vs. Gemini 1.5 Pro), it is best to check the official documentation for the exact numbers.* However, as a general rule of thumb:\n*   **Gemini Flash models** usually offer higher rate limits because they are optimized for speed and efficiency.\n*   **Gemini Pro models** often have stricter rate limits due to the heavier computing power required for complex reasoning.\n\n### How to Check Exact Limits\nYou can find the exact, up-to-date rate limits for your account by checking the **Google AI Studio pricing and limits page** or the **Google Cloud Vertex AI documentation**, depending on where you manage your API keys. \n\nIf you hit a rate limit, the API will typically return a `429 Too Many Requests` error, meaning your application needs to pause briefly or implement a \"retry with backoff\" strategy.','2026-10-15 08:57:53','2026-10-15 08:57:53',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'null',0),(361,10,'user','What skills are mentioned in resume?','2026-10-15 08:59:08','2026-10-15 08:59:08',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'null',0),(362,10,'assistant','Based on the provided document, the skills mentioned in the resume are:\n\n* **Frontend Development:** HTML5, CSS3, Bootstrap 5, React.js, JavaScript\n* **Backend Development:** Node.js, Express.js, Python, Django, RESTful APIs\n* **Databases:** MongoDB, Mongoose, PostgreSQL, Supabase, MS SQL Server, SQLite\n* **Authentication & Security:** JWT, bcrypt, Cookie-Based Authentication, Supabase Auth, Role-Based Access Control (RBAC), Row Level Security (RLS)\n* **Real-Time Technologies:** Socket.IO, Supabase Realtime, WebRTC\n* **Programming Languages:** C, C++, C#, JavaScript, Python\n* **Tools & Platforms:** Git, GitHub, VS Code, Postman','2026-10-15 08:59:15','2026-10-15 08:59:15',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'null',0),(363,11,'user','gemini api rate limit','2026-10-15 08:59:38','2026-10-15 08:59:38',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'null',0),(364,11,'assistant','I am not sure about the Gemini API rate limits, as that information is not provided in the document.','2026-10-15 08:59:51','2026-10-15 08:59:51',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'null',0),(365,11,'user','what is the gemini api rate limit','2026-10-15 09:00:17','2026-10-15 09:00:17',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'null',0),(366,11,'assistant','Gemini API rate limits depend on the specific tier you are using (such as the Free tier or a Pay-as-you-go / Paid tier) and the specific model you are calling (like Gemini 1.5 Flash or Gemini 1.5 Pro). \n\nHere is a general breakdown of how limits work:\n\n1. **Free Tier:** Typically limited to a certain number of requests per minute (RPM) and requests per day (RPD). For example, many of the free models allow around 15 requests per minute and a daily cap (such as 1,500 requests per day).\n2. **Paid Tier (Pay-as-you-go):** Offers much higher limits (often hundreds or thousands of requests per minute) designed for production applications, billed based on your token usage.\n3. **Token Limits:** In addition to request counts, there are limits on how many tokens (words/characters) you can send per minute (TPM).\n\nBecause Google frequently updates these limits and they vary by region and model, the best and most accurate place to check the exact current limits is the official [Google AI for Developers documentation and pricing page](https://ai.google.dev/pricing).','2026-10-15 09:00:23','2026-10-15 09:00:23',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'null',0),(367,11,'user','What skills are mentioned?','2026-10-15 09:00:36','2026-10-15 09:00:36',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'null',0),(368,11,'assistant','Based on the provided document, the following technical skills are mentioned:\n\n* **Frontend Development:** HTML5, CSS3, Bootstrap 5, React.js, JavaScript\n* **Backend Development:** Node.js, Express.js, Python, Django, RESTful APIs\n* **Databases:** MongoDB, Mongoose, PostgreSQL, Supabase, MS SQL Server, SQLite\n* **Authentication & Security:** JWT, bcrypt, Cookie-Based Authentication, Supabase Auth, Role-Based Access Control (RBAC), Row Level Security (RLS)\n* **Real-Time Technologies:** Socket.IO, Supabase Realtime, WebRTC\n* **Programming Languages:** C, C++, C#, JavaScript, Python\n* **Tools & Platforms:** Git, GitHub, VS Code, Postman','2026-10-15 09:00:43','2026-10-15 09:00:43',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'null',0),(369,11,'user','이력서에 어떤 학력 사항이 언급되어 있나요?','2026-10-15 09:01:47','2026-10-15 09:01:47',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'null',0),(370,11,'assistant','제공된 문서에 따르면, 다음과 같은 학력 사항이 언급되어 있습니다:\n\n* **학위:** 정보공학 기술학사 (Bachelor of Information Engineering Technology)\n* **학교:** 슈페리어 대학교 (Superior University, 파키스탄 라호르)\n* **재학 기간:** 2021년 – 2025년\n* **학점:** CGPA 3.48 / 4.00','2026-10-15 09:01:52','2026-10-15 09:01:52',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'null',0),(371,