verage your skills in the MERN/MEAN stacks, Python/Django, and AI technologies to contribute to impactful tech projects.\n*   **Education:** You are pursuing a Bachelor of Science in Computer Science (BSCS) from the University of Gujrat, expected to graduate around 2026.\n*   **Technical Skills:** \n    *   *Frontend:* HTML5, CSS3, JavaScript, React.js, Bootstrap 5.\n    *   *Backend:* Node.js, Express.js, Python, Django.\n    *   *Databases & Tools:* MongoDB, PostgreSQL, SQLite, Supabase, Git, GitHub, RESTful APIs, WebRTC.\n*   **Projects:** You have built four notable projects:\n    1. **Facebook Clone** (Full-stack social media app using React and Supabase).\n    2. **Real-Time Chat Application** (Built with the MERN stack and WebRTC).\n    3. **Task / To-Do Application** (Features file uploads and a statistics dashboard).\n    4. **ResumEase — AI-Powered HR Assistant** (Built with Python, Django, and AI/ML tech).\n*   **Certifications:** You hold certifications in JavaScript Full Stack / Web Development (NAVTTC), AI Fundamentals (Cisco / IBM SkillsBuild), and Advanced JavaScript & Full Stack Development (Centre for Digital Literacy & Business Management).','2026-10-21 08:12:37','2026-10-21 08:12:37',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'null',0),(529,18,'user','Experience in resume','2026-10-21 08:13:26','2026-10-21 08:13:26',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'null',0),(530,18,'assistant','Based on the provided document, here is the professional experience listed in your resume:\n\n*   **Current Role:** MERN Stack Developer Intern at ArhamSoft\n    *   *Details:* You are currently gaining hands-on, professional experience in full-stack web development at ArhamSoft.','2026-10-21 08:13:29','2026-10-21 08:13:29',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'null',0),(531,18,'user','Facebook Clone','2026-10-21 08:14:38','2026-10-21 08:14:38',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'null',0),(532,18,'assistant','Based on the provided document, here are the details for the **Facebook Clone — Full Stack Social Media Application**:\n\n*   **Technologies Used:** React.js, Supabase, PostgreSQL, Supabase Auth, Supabase Realtime, Supabase Storage, Row Level Security (RLS), and Bootstrap 5.\n*   **Key Features & Responsibilities:**\n    *   Developed a full-stack social media platform featuring user authentication, user profiles, posts, comments, friendships, messaging, and notifications.\n    *   Implemented post management features, including privacy settings, likes, saves, shares, comments, replies, and mentions.\n    *   Developed social interaction functionalities such as friend requests and user blocking.\n    *   Integrated Supabase Realtime to power instant messaging and real-time notifications.\n    *   Implemented user reporting and administrative moderation features, including the ability to suspend and restore accounts.\n    *   Secured application data and controlled access using PostgreSQL, Supabase Storage, Row Level Security (RLS), and protected routes.','2026-10-21 08:14:41','2026-10-21 08:14:41',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'null',0),(533,18,'user','What is RLS','2026-10-21 08:15:13','2026-10-21 08:15:13',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'null',0),(534,18,'assistant','**RLS** stands for **Row Level Security**. \n\nThink of it as a security guard stationed at a database table. Normally, if a user has permission to look at a database, they can see *all* the rows of data inside a table. RLS allows you to set rules so that users can only see or modify the specific rows of data that belong to them or that they are explicitly allowed to access.\n\n### How it works with a simple example:\nImagine you have a notes app, and all users store their notes in the same database table. \n* **Without RLS:** If User A runs a query to look at the notes table, the database might accidentally show them User B\'s private notes.\n* **With RLS:** You create a rule that says: *\"Only show a row of data if the `user_id` on that row matches the ID of the person currently logged in.\"* This way, User A can only ever see their own notes, keeping everyone\'s data private and secure. \n\nIn your resume project (the Facebook Clone), RLS is used alongside PostgreSQL and Supabase to secure application data and control who has access to what.','2026-10-21 08:15:17','2026-10-21 08:15:17',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'null',0),(535,18,'user','Score thresholding','2026-10-21 08:15:46','2026-10-21 08:15:46',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'null',0),(536,18,'assistant','**Score thresholding** is a technique used in computer science, machine learning, and data processing to filter out low-quality results by setting a minimum cutoff point (a \"threshold\"). \n\nThink of it like a bouncer at a club door who has a rule: *\"Guests must be at least 18 years old to enter.\"* Anyone under 18 is turned away, and only those meeting or exceeding the age limit are let in.\n\n### How it works:\n1. **Scoring:** An algorithm, AI model, or search engine evaluates a set of items and gives each one a score based on how confident it is, how relevant it is, or how well it matches a condition. (For example, a score from 0 to 1, or 0% to 100%).\n2. **Setting the Threshold:** You decide on a specific number as your baseline (the threshold), such as `0.75` (or 75%).\n3. **Filtering:** Anything scoring *below* 0.75 is discarded or ignored. Only items scoring *0.75 or higher* are kept.\n\n### Common Examples:\n* **Spam Filters:** An email filter calculates a \"spam score\" for incoming messages. If the score is above `0.80`, it goes straight to the spam folder. If it\'s below, it goes to your inbox.\n* **Facial Recognition:** A security camera scans a face and compares it to a database. It might calculate a 92% match. If the threshold is set to 85%, it successfully unlocks the door. If it only matches by 60%, it rejects the entry.\n* **Search & AI:** When an AI searches a database for answers, score thresholding ensures it only returns results that are actually relevant, preventing it from giving you random, low-quality guesses. \n\nIn short, score thresholding is a way to separate the \"good enough\" results from the noise.','2026-10-21 08:15:51','2026-10-21 08:15:51',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'null',0),(537,18,'user','What are all the projects mentioned in my resume?','2026-10-22 11:00:37','2026-10-22 11:00:37',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'null',0),(538,18,'assistant','Based on the provided document chunks, here are all the projects mentioned in your resume:\n\n1. **Facebook Clone** — Full Stack Social Media Application\n   * **Technologies:** React.js, Supabase, PostgreSQL, Supabase Auth, Supabase Realtime, Supabase Storage, RLS, Bootstrap 5\n2. **Real-Time Chat Application** — MERN Stack & WebRTC *(Note: The detailed description for this project and the Task / To-Do Application are cut off in the provided text chunks, but they are listed as projects).*\n3. **Task / To-Do Application** *(Note: The document mentions features for this project like Multer integration and an interactive dashboard, but the full title and technologies are cut off in the available text).*\n4. **ResumEase** — AI-Powered HR Assistant\n   * **Technologies:** Python, Django, HTML5, CSS3, Bootstrap 5, JavaScript, SQLite, AI/ML','2026-10-22 11:00:41','2026-10-22 11:00:41',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'null',0),(539,19,'user','What are all the projects mentioned in my resume?','2026-10-22 11:03:30','2026-10-22 11:03:30',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'null',0),(540,19,'assistant','It looks like you haven\'t uploaded or provided your resume yet! \n\nPlease upload your resume file, and I will be happy to read through it and list all the projects mentioned.','2026-10-22 11:03:31','2026-10-22 11:03:31',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'null',0),(541,19,'user','What are all the projects mentioned in my resume?','2026-10-22 11:12:14','2026-10-22 11:12:14',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'null',0),(542,19,'assistant','Based on the provided document, the projects mentioned in 